;; Malaysia national holidays 2008-2040: external gold for MY.
;; Regenerate: uv run --no-project --with holidays==0.109 python -I scripts/generate_asia_holiday_gold.py MY
;; :days lists every holiday as (YEAR MONTH DAY NAME); any other day is not one.
(
 :country "MY"
 :generated "2026-11-27"
 :from 2008 :to 2040
 :note "Federal public holidays (Holidays Act 1951 First Schedule; the JPM Jadual Hari Kelepasan Am Persekutuan of each year 2008-2027 with its amendments, and the s. 8 additional days), with the s. 3 replacement for a holiday on a Sunday. State and Federal Territory days are not in it. 2028-2040 are provisional: fixed days and estimates (tabular Islamic dates; lunar 1/1 and 4/15 from the HKO tables; Deepavali the day before the first new moon, IST, after 17 October; the Agong's birthday the first Monday of June)."
 :sources
 (
  (:title "Holidays Act 1951 (Act 369), ss. 1(2), 2, 3, 8, 9 and First Schedule (Akta Hari Kelepasan 1951)" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/2024id_/http://www.kabinet.gov.my/bkpp/pdf/akta_warta/1951_12_31_act369.pdf"
   :text "s. 3: a public holiday that falls on a weekly holiday (Sunday, or Friday where Friday is the weekly holiday): the day following is a public holiday, and if that day is already one, the day after. First Schedule: Maulidur Rasul, National Day, Chinese New Year (2 days; 1 in Kelantan and Terengganu), Wesak, the Agong's birthday, Hari Raya Puasa (2 days), Hari Raya Haji (1 day; 2 in Kelantan and Terengganu), Deepavali, Christmas; Labour Day (P.U.(B) 414/1972), Awal Muharam (P.U.(B) 363/2005), Malaysia Day (P.U.(B) 491/2009, from 2010).")
  (:title "JPM / BKPP Jadual Hari Kelepasan Am Persekutuan 2008-2027 (kabinet.gov.my; Wayback copies)" :uri "https://www.kabinet.gov.my/storage/2026/08/HKA_2027.pdf"
   :text "The federal table of each year; every date below is the table's, with its gazetted amendments (Deepavali 2014: Warta No. 43367; Awal Muharam 2017: Warta No. 1779; the Agong's birthday 2020: Warta No. 6489; Hari Raya Puasa 2022: PMO statement of 1 May 2022). Deepavali is not a Sarawak holiday and CNY day 2 not a Kelantan / Terengganu one; both are federal days.")
  (:title "Warta Kerajaan Persekutuan: Jadual Hari Kelepasan Am Persekutuan 2019-2025" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/2024id_/http://www.kabinet.gov.my/bkpp/pdf/akta_warta/20230810_HARI_KELEPASAN_2024.pdf"
   :text "Pemberitahuan No. 17295 (2019), 12985 (2020), 16872 (2023), 19239 (2024), 17852 (2025); the 2021 and 2022 tables of 9 July 2020 and 24 June 2021.")
  (:title "Holidays Act 1951 s. 8 notifications: additional public holidays" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/2022id_/http://www.kabinet.gov.my/bkpp/pdf/akta_warta/20221114_PUB556.pdf"
   :text "P.U.(B) 70/2012 (11 April 2012), 176/2017 (24 April 2017), 325/2019 (30 July 2019), 556/2022 (18-19 November 2022), 579/2022 (28 November 2022), 154/2023 (21 April 2023), 305/2025 (15 September 2025); 9 May 2018 (PMO statement of 11 April 2018); 4 September 2017 and 10-11 May 2018 as announced (no P.U.(B) copy was archived).")
  (:title "PMO statement, 1 May 2022: the s. 3 replacement days" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20220515191737id_/https://www.pmo.gov.my/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/152022-KENYATAAN-MEDIA-PERUBAHAN-CUTI-UMUM.pdf"
   :text "Hari Raya Aidilfitri on Monday 2 May 2022; Labour Day (Sunday 1 May) replaced on Wednesday 4 May under s. 3, except in Kedah, Kelantan, Terengganu and Johor.")
  (:title "JPM, 31 July 2024: no replacement day for Malaysia Day and Maulidur Rasul on 16 September 2024" :uri "https://www.thestar.com.my/news/nation/2024/08/02/no-automatic-replacement-holiday-on-sept-17"
   :text "Two holidays on one weekday give no extra day: s. 3 covers only a holiday on the weekly holiday.")
 )
